{title: Higher}
{song_number: 73}
{language: en}
{tempo: 72}
{comment: Verse}
[A]Who gives orders to the morning, tells the sun [D]where to [A]rise;
[D]who speaks life into existence, tells the dark [F#m7]where to reside?
[E]Who chose to [A]love the unloving, told the crippled to [D]rise up;
[D]who chose to die for my [F#m7]redemption, came to mend the [D]broken [E]hearts?
[D]There is no one like our [A]God.
{comment: Chorus}
[E]None like You. You are [A]higher, higher than the heavens,
[Esus4]and Your love, Your love [E]deeper than the oceans,
[A]and Your word, Your word, [F#m]true until the [E]end,
[A]so I am holding on [D]to You, [Esus4]the [E]Author of [A]life.

{comment: Bridge}

[A]Jesus, it's You,, name above all names,
[D]worthy of all praise, beyond all I know.
[E]I’ll never be able to fathom Your ways.
[A]And though I can't see You, my heart knows You well. Jesus, You're higher.
{comment: Order: verse, chorus, bridge, chorus.}
